.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt WRITE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm write
.Nd send a message to another user's terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar user
.Op Ar tty
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility sends the text read from the terminal to another user. It checks that
the user exists, has a logged-in terminal and has not disabled messages with
.Ql mesg n .
Lines are sent with terminal CRLF endings.
.Pp
The target image has one console terminal; the host tests exercise the
unknown-user, not-logged-in and
.Ql mesg n
refusal paths through the directory/terminal seams.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An unknown user, no logged-in terminal, disabled messages or a write failure
exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr more 1 ,
.Xr who 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the documented POSIX write subset.
